description:
Summary: Updates internal docs site content for rollout policies to include the new SLO-based auto-rollback/pause feature (behind flag), and links the authoritative Confluence runbook + metrics naming standard + ADRs. Adds concrete policy config JSON examples (per-tier templates + per-rollout override) and clarifies semantics around debounce/min-sample + monitor staleness handling.

Context: As we ship auto-mitigation for rollout regressions, multiple teams asked for a single “how do I enable it safely?” page that points to the runbook and the canonical metric/labeling standard. This PR is documentation-only; no code behavior changes.

What changed (high level):
- Added a new section to rollout policies docs: “Auto actions on SLO breach (pause/rollback)”.
- Linked to Confluence artifacts used by oncall and standards owners:
  - Runbook: Auto-rollback on SLO breach (triage + override + restart rollout)
  - Observability standard: rollouts/SLO metrics naming + labels + cardinality guidance
  - ADRs: breach evaluation/debounce strategy, audit trail schema
- Added examples of policy configuration JSON with safe defaults and guardrails.
- Added a short FAQ that answers “why didn’t it rollback?” (suppressed, missing/stale monitor, min sample not met, in incident override).

Docs links (internal):
- Runbook: https://confluence.redwoodinference.com/display/ENGSRE/Auto-rollback+on+SLO+breach+runbook
- Metrics naming/labels: https://confluence.redwoodinference.com/display/ARCH/rollouts-slo-metrics-naming-and-labeling
- ADR-0127: https://confluence.redwoodinference.com/display/ARCH/ADR-0127+SLO+breach+evaluation+and+debounce
- ADR-0128: https://confluence.redwoodinference.com/display/ARCH/ADR-0128+Rollout+audit+trail+schema+for+auto+actions

Policy config examples added (snippets):

Example A — service default template (Dedicated tier) with rollback enabled:
{
  "rollouts": {
    "autoActions": {
      "enabled": true,
      "mode": "rollback",
      "signals": {
        "latency_p99": {
          "slo": "p99_latency",
          "burnRate": {
            "fastWindow": "5m",
            "fastThreshold": 14,
            "slowWindow": "30m",
            "slowThreshold": 6
          },
          "minSamples": {
            "requests": 2000,
            "window": "10m"
          }
        },
        "error_rate": {
          "slo": "5xx_rate",
          "burnRate": {
            "fastWindow": "5m",
            "fastThreshold": 10,
            "slowWindow": "30m",
            "slowThreshold": 4
          },
          "minSamples": {
            "requests": 1000,
            "window": "10m"
          }
        }
      },
      "debounce": {
        "holdoffAfterStepChange": "4m",
        "cooldownAfterAction": "20m"
      },
      "monitorHealth": {
        "maxStaleness": "3m",
        "onMissingOrStale": "pause"
      },
      "suppressions": {
        "allowManualSuppression": true,
        "maxSuppressionDuration": "2h"
      }
    }
  }
}

Example B — per-rollout override: pause-only + tighter staleness handling for a high-risk change:
{
  "rolloutOverrides": {
    "autoActions": {
      "enabled": true,
      "mode": "pause",
      "debounce": {
        "holdoffAfterStepChange": "6m"
      },
      "monitorHealth": {
        "maxStaleness": "90s",
        "onMissingOrStale": "pause"
      }
    }
  }
}

Notes in docs:
- The JSON keys above reflect the policy engine schema introduced in the rollout auto-rollback work; field names are written to match the current implementation used by Console/policy bundles.
- “mode=rollback” rolls back to last known-good step/model version; “mode=pause” holds the rollout at current step and requires an explicit resume.
- We explicitly document guardrails to avoid oscillation: dual-window confirmation + min sample gating + cooldown.

Checklist:
- [x] Links validated against current Confluence page IDs
- [x] Example JSON reviewed by policy engine owner (Benji)
- [x] SRE wording reviewed for oncall clarity (Sean)
- [x] Metrics/labels wording reviewed against standard (Allison)

Follow-ups (not in this PR):
- Add a short Console UI screenshot once DES-944 lands and the UI stabilizes.
- Add a “pre-flight enablement checklist” page (release gates) once ENG-4850 is complete.
